{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.ComplexMassConstituentFunctional","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.ComplexMassConstituentFunctional","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Complex.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.charm_block_determined","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.charm_block_determined","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/complex-mass-constituent-functional.lean#L87-L95","doc":"**Conditional consequence (sorry-free).** Given the conjecture, the\nsecond-generation (charm, `n = 5`) block of any state is the fixed continuant\nratio `contRatio 5` times its first-generation (`n = 3`) block: the heavy\nvalue is *determined* by the light one, no free parameter. Proved from\n`tower_law` at `n = 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassConstituent.light_anchor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassConstituent.light_anchor","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/complex-mass-constituent-functional.lean#L83-L83","doc":"**Light-doublet anchor.** The first-generation (`n = 3`) real-part\nsplitting between the up and down states reproduces the substrate-fixed\ndoublet splitting `deltaUD / ℏ_q²` — the one calibrated handle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassConstituent.tower_law","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassConstituent.tower_law","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/complex-mass-constituent-functional.lean#L78-L78","doc":"**No-tuning winding-tower law.** The functional on the generation-`(n+2)`\nblock equals the fixed continuant ratio times the generation-`n` block\n(`2 ≤ n`: the tower starts at the first physical generation `n = 3`). This\nis the falsifiable \"one functional, no per-flavour knob\" content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassConstituent.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassConstituent.mk","kind":"ctor","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/complex-mass-constituent-functional.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassConstituent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassConstituent","kind":"class","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/complex-mass-constituent-functional.lean#L66-L85","doc":"**Primary conjecture — complex-mass constituent functional.**\n\nA single complex-mass functional `M` realizes the light quark doublet *and*\ndetermines the heavy-flavour blocks with no per-flavour tuning: successive\ngenerations are tied by the fixed continuant ratio (`tower_law`), and the\nfirst-generation real-part splitting reproduces the substrate-fixed doublet\nsplitting (`light_anchor`). Primary/open: no instance is exhibited. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:complex-mass-constituent-functional","label":"conj:complex-mass-constituent-functional","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/complex-mass-constituent-functional.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassData.deltaUD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassData.deltaUD","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/complex-mass-constituent-functional.lean#L64-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassData.down","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassData.down","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/complex-mass-constituent-functional.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassData.up","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassData.up","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/complex-mass-constituent-functional.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassData.hbarQSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassData.hbarQSq","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/complex-mass-constituent-functional.lean#L61-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassData.contRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassData.contRatio","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/complex-mass-constituent-functional.lean#L60-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassData.proj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassData.proj","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/complex-mass-constituent-functional.lean#L59-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassData.M","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassData.M","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/complex-mass-constituent-functional.lean#L58-L58","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassData.State","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassData.State","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/complex-mass-constituent-functional.lean#L57-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/complex-mass-constituent-functional.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ComplexMassData","kind":"structure","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/complex-mass-constituent-functional.lean#L44-L64","doc":"Archimedean data for the complex-mass constituent functional.\n\n* `State`     — composite-braid / Hecke-module states.\n* `M`         — the complex-mass functional `𝔐` (complex-volume-weighted trace):\n  `Re` is a mass, `Im` the confinement / instability scale.\n* `proj n`    — selects the generation-`n` flavour block (`n = 3, 5, 7` for the\n  three generations, the torus-knot longitudinal windings).\n* `contRatio n` — the winding-tower ratio `b_n / b_{n-2}` of the Morgan–Voyce /\n  Fibonacci continuants: **fixed by the substrate tower, not a per-flavour knob**.\n* `up`, `down` — the two first-generation (light-doublet) states.\n* `hbarQSq`   — the substrate factor `ℏ_q²`.\n* `deltaUD`   — the substrate-fixed up–down splitting (an input). ","signatureChunk":0}]}